      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Balancing these perspectives on economic sanctions involves considering both their effectiveness and the intentions behind their application. In some cases, sanctions have indeed pressured regimes towards reforms and accountability, sometimes leading to positive outcomes like the promotion of democracy. However, sanctions can also be used as leverage by powerful countries to exert control over weaker states, often leading to unintended consequences. The ethical and practical impact of sanctions significantly varies based on the specific context and intentions of the applying country. Researching case studies from different situations can help clarify these differing perspectives.",
